# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, four kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order. The
#                                  folder is named as it sits in CLAUDE/Plan/, with no
#                                  CLAUDE/Plan/ in front (00123-name, not CLAUDE/Plan/00123-name)
#   playbooks/<path>.yml [args]    a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand. Words after
#                                  it are ansible-playbook arguments: name the play's tags
#                                  (--tags lightning) so only the changed part runs. A
#                                  tagged run never decides the play's state, so a later
#                                  changed-plays still runs the play in full if it is due
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry, except
#                                  that a script named *acceptance*.bash may exit 2 for
#                                  COULD NOT ESTABLISH, as an acceptance.bash may
#   changed-plays                  every play that has run here and has to run again, as
#                                  one unit: the checkout's ./run.bash --changed --yes, in
#                                  playbook-main.yml order, stopping at the first failure
#
# changed-plays runs WHERE IT STANDS in the list, like every other entry, and decides which
# plays it runs when it starts, so the entries above it have already run (a play an entry
# above ran is no longer changed, and is not run twice). Put it above the plan entries whose
# deploy or acceptance expects the changed plays to have run, which is the usual case, and
# below an entry it must follow. It replaces a hand-copied list of stale plays: name a
# playbooks/ entry only for a play that must run at a fixed point between two plan steps.
# Its description says which changed plays the agent expects it to pick up and why.
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Issue #295: the raw-prune fix (it could delete a RAW whose JPG sat in a folder it could not
# read). changed-plays did not deploy it: play-photography has no play-ledger record on this
# host, so --changed never judges it (issue #323). The deployed clip-scan is stale too. The
# whole play runs, so the ledger records it and a later changed-plays judges it. Expected:
# changed for ~/.local/bin/raw-prune and ~/.local/bin/clip-scan; RapidRAW and ART unchanged.
# Afterwards: sha256sum of each deployed copy matches its files/home/.local/bin/ source.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-photography.yml
# Issue #323 sweep: play-advanced-kernel-management has no play-ledger record here either, and
# its deployed manage-kernel-versions.py and service unit are older than the checkout. Neither
# change alters which kernels are kept: the script now names the kernel's arch from the machine
# instead of a fixed x86_64 (the same argv on x86_64), and the service starts after
# multi-user.target so boot no longer waits on dnf (issue #263). installonly_limit=3 is already
# set. The play's own initial analysis run follows, as on every run. Expected: changed for the
# script and the service, a systemd reload; versionlocks as the analysis reports them.
# Afterwards: both deployed files match the checkout (the service rendered).
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-advanced-kernel-management.yml

# Issue #260 (ccy 3.122.17, container 2.84.25): pingbus, teamchat and the launcher never wait
# in silence on stdin. Installs the launcher; the image carries helpers/stdin_text and the
# rebuilt pingbus and teamchat, and is rebuilt once at the next ccy start. pingbus's
# thread --close reads no stdin unless --note - is given; a text verb (say, reply, report)
# refuses a terminal, says on stderr after a second that it is waiting, and exits 64 if nothing
# has come within 60 s. Afterwards: a new ccy session starts, on container 2.84.25.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml

# Issue #260: the agent-bus member kit carries the same pingbus. Expected: changed for the
# kit's pingbus and its helpers/stdin_text.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml

# Issue #260: the lab's vmtest modules read stdin through helpers/stdin_text, which says on
# stderr when it is waiting for input that has not ended; the play now deploys it beside them.
# Expected: changed for the vmtest modules that read stdin and the new stdin_text directory;
# skip this entry on a host without the lab.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-vm-test-lab.yml

# Issue #260: every other play whose inputs changed (the Go commands built from
# internal/stdinread and internal/ui: teamchat-admin, ccy-teams and the hooks). Those the
# entries above ran are not due again. Afterwards report what changed.
changed-plays
